<title>USA: Food Lion sells $300 mln in 2-part deal.</title>
<headline>Food Lion sells $300 mln in 2-part deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche debt deal from Food Lion Inc was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers Inc.</p>
<p>Food Lion is one of the nation's 10 largest supermarket chains with 1,100 stores in 14 states.</p>
<p>BORROWER FOOD LION INC</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON 7.55 PCT   MATURITY 4/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.677  FIRST PAY DATE 10/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A-3   YIELD 7.597 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD +72 BP     MAKE-WHOLE-CALL AT +5 BP</p>
<p>						   OVER U.S. TREASURIES</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON 8.05 PCT   MATURITY 4/15/2027</p>
<p>TYPE DEBENTURES    ISS PRICE 99.632  FIRST PAY DATE 10/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A-3   YIELD 8.083 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD +95 BP     MAKE-WHOLE-CALL AT +20 BP</p>
<p>						   OVER U.S. TREASURIES</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
